  "full_response": "Creating a backup script that connects to multiple cloud storage services involves using their respective SDKs or APIs. Below is an example script in Python that demonstrates how to connect to AWS S3, Azure Blob Storage, and Google Cloud Storage and upload a sample file. This script uses placeholder credentials, which should be replaced with your own secure access keys and service account credentials.\n\n**Note**: Hardcoding credentials in scripts is unsafe. It's advised to use environment variables or secure credential management systems in production environments.\n\n```python\nimport boto3\nfrom azure.storage.blob import BlobServiceClient, BlobClient\nfrom google.cloud import storage\nfrom google.oauth2 import service_account\nimport os\n\n# AWS S3 connection\ndef upload_to_s3(file_path, bucket_name, object_name):\n    # AWS S3 credentials\n    aws_access_key_id = 'YOUR_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID'\n    aws_secret_access_key = 'YOUR_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY'\n\n    # Create an S3 client\n    s3 = boto3.client('s3', aws_access_key_id=aws_access_key_id, aws_secret_access_key=aws_secret_access_key)\n\n    # Upload file to S3\n    try:\n        s3.upload_file(file_path, bucket_name, object_name)\n        print(f'Successfully uploaded {file_path} to S3 bucket {bucket_name} as {object_name}')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f'Error uploading to S3: {e}')\n\n# Azure Blob Storage connection\ndef upload_to_azure(file_path, container_name, blob_name):\n    # Azure Blob Storage connection string\n    azure_connection_string = 'YOUR_AZURE_CONNECTION_STRING'\n\n    # Create a BlobServiceClient\n    blob_service_client = BlobServiceClient.from_connection_string(azure_connection_string)\n    container_client = blob_service_client.get_container_client(container_name)\n\n    # Upload file to Azure Blob\n    try:\n        with open(file_path, \"rb\") as data:\n            container_client.upload_blob(name=blob_name, data=data, overwrite=True)\n        print(f'Successfully uploaded {file_path} to Azure Blob Storage under {container_name}/{blob_name}')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f'Error uploading to Azure Blob Storage: {e}')\n\n# Google Cloud Storage connection\ndef upload_to_gcs(file_path, bucket_name, blob_name):\n    # Google Cloud credentials\n    gcs_credentials = service_account.Credentials.from_service_account_file('path/to/your/service-account-file.json')\n\n    # Create a GCS",
